      "published_at": "2026-10-16T14:00:00+00:00",
      "snippet": "We estimate that U.S. generation from small-scale or rooftop solar photovoltaic systems (smaller than 1 megawatt of capacity) has increased from 18,812 gigawatthours (GWh) to 92,979 GWh over the last decade. The four states with the highest generation of small-scale solar in the country-California, Arizona, Texas, and Florida-are in regions with more abundant solar resources. Even though it is in a region with lower solar resources, New York ranks as the fifth-largest rooftop solar generation pr",
      "source": "U.S. EIA Today in Energy",
      "title": "U.S. small-scale solar generation has quadrupled in the last decade",
      "url": "https://www.eia.gov/todayinenergy/detail.php?id=68324"
